  <content>
    <section>
      <div class="os-raise-familysupport">
        <para><link url="https://phet.colorado.edu/sims/html/area-model-algebra/latest/area-model-algebra_en.html?screens=1,2,3">Access the interactive simulator </link>to begin this project.</para>
      </div>
      <para>In this activity, whenever you see 💬, stop and share your responses with your partner. If you have different responses, try to come to a consensus.</para>
      <para>For 1 - 8, use the following instructions.</para>
      <para>
        <quote>Use the simulation screen labeled “Explore”. Note you can switch between simulation screens using the toolbar located below the area model.</quote>
     </para>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
        <newline/>
        <item>Explain what the red and blue sliders do to the outside of the rectangle.</item>
        <newline/>
        <item>Explain what the red and blue sliders do to the inside of the rectangle.</item>
        <newline/>
        <item>Describe what changes and what doesn’t change when the red and blue sliders are moved. 💬</item>
        <newline/>
        <item>
        Multiply 10✕15 using an area model. Find two different ways to partition the 10x15 rectangle. Use the sim to support you in filling out this table. 💬
   </item>
        <table class="os-raise-wideadjustedtable">
          <tgroup cols="4"><tbody><row>
              <entry>
                <emphasis>Problem</emphasis>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <emphasis>Labeled Area Model with Partial Products</emphasis>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <emphasis>List partial products and write as a sum</emphasis>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <emphasis>Total area of rectangle</emphasis>
              </entry>
            </row>
          <row>
              <entry>
                <para>10✕15</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para>
                  <figure>
                    <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                      <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_07_03_03_01.png"/>
                    </media>
                  </figure>
               </para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <newline/>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <newline/>
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <para>10✕15</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para>
                  <figure>
                    <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
                      <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_07_03_03_02.png"/>
                    </media>
                  </figure>
               </para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <newline/>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <newline/>
              </entry>
            </row>
          </tbody></tgroup></table>
        <newline/>
        <item>Use the sim to model 6✕18. What is the total area of this rectangle? Represent the total area in multiple ways.</item>
        <figure>
          <media alt="Insert Alt Text">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_07_03_03_03.png"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
        <newline/>
        <item>In an area model, how do the partial products (interior numbers) get calculated?</item>
        <newline/>
        <item>In an area model, what are two different ways the total area could get calculated?</item>
        <newline/>
        <item>How do the partial products relate to the total area of the area model?</item>
      </list>
    </section>
